# L §7.3 The error bound: "a transcendental whose argument is itself an interval takes the hull of its exact
# values over that interval, then its own ± u/2"; "The bound prints to two significant digits, rounded up".
# r = exp(2) to 1e-9 lies within 5e-10 of e^2 (7.389...), so ln over [r - 5e-10, r + 5e-10] lies within
# (5e-10 + |r - e^2|)/7.38 < 1.4e-10 of 2; ln(r) itself is within 1e-10 of 2, so it rounds to 2 on 1e-6.  The
# bound is 5e-7 plus that hull's half-width, more than 5.0e-7 and less than 5.1e-7: printed 0.00000051.
=== m.tally
model t
  tally 2
  on 2026-12-31
  start 2026-01-01
  end 2026-12-31

source s "s"
unit PLN: currency minor 0.01

input two: num
def l2: num = ln(exp(two) to 1e-9) to 1e-6 at reader

version v
  cite s
  governs 2026..
  known 2026-01-01
  two = 2

ask a: l2 law 2026-06-30
=== expect
a: ≈ 2 ± 0.00000051
  law date 2026-06-30, cut 2026-12-31
